AB  - As industrial artificial intelligence (AI) applications become increasingly prevalent and the performance of neural processing unit (NPU) is advanced continuously, deploying lightweight networks on NPU has become a favorable option for high real-time industrial scenarios, including autonomous driving, intelligent mine, and more. However, common lightweight networks are not primarily designed for NPU, thereby failing to fully leverage the performance of NPU. In this paper, an NPU lightweight network, called Efficient Large Kernel Convolution Network (ELKCNet) is proposed for downstream tasks, such as semantic segmentation and object detection, which have broad application scenarios and significant potential. By incorporating a portion of large kernel convolutions into the Efficient Large Kernel Convolution (ELKC) block, the network’s receptive field is further enhanced to capture richer contextual information and effectively integrate local and global features. To explore the operational principles of NPU, a design paradigm for NPU lightweight networks is proposed. By testing the inference times of various convolutions and pooling operations on NPU, data support is provided for optimizing and constructing novel NPU lightweight networks. To validate the superiority of the ELKCNet, comparative experiments are conducted on multiple datasets, showing that it outperforms other lightweight networks in object detection and semantic segmentation. Additionally, the ELKCNet is evaluated on the underground mine semantic segmentation dataset to further demonstrate its effectiveness and significant potential in real-time industrial applications.
ER  - 

